	(text "1)	THIS IS A 2 LAYER BOARD\n\n2)	THIS BOARD IS NOT IMPEDANCE CONTROLLED.\n\n3)	IF CONNECTING TO AN OLDER REVISION OF THE STANDBY CONTROLLER,\n	THAT IS NOT EQUIPT WITH \"nSLEEP\" OF \"nFAULT\", CONNECT \"nSLEEP\"\n	TO +5V TO ENABLE THE STEPPER DRIVER.  STARTING WITH THE 2.0.0 REV,\n	THESE LINES ARE INTEGRATED AND NOTHING FURTHER IS REQUIRED.\n\n4)	WARNING - INTERCONNECT HARNESS CONSTRUCTION\n	DEPENDING ON YOUR REVISION OF THE GAUGE PCBS CONSTRUCTED, NOT\n	ALL PINS ON THE GAUGE HEADERS WILL BE CONNECTED. REFER TO THE\n	GAUGE PCB SCHEMATIC TO HELP CROSS REFERENCE WIRING. PIN NAMES\n	MAY NOT BE CONSISTANT BETWEEN CONTROLLER AND GAUGE PCBS.\n	PAY CLOSE ATTENTION TO STEPPER MOTOR CONNECTIONS\n	PIN PAIRS ARE AS FOLLOWS:\n	COIL 1: IN1 & IN2\n	COIL 2: IN3 & IN4\n	CAUTION: DO NOT SWAP A PIN FROM COIL 1 & 2 TO THE OPPOSING COIL\n	UNPREDICATABLE RESULTS WILL OCCUR.\n	IT MAY BE NEEDED TO SWAP PINS WITHIN A COIL DEPENDING ON THE\n	SPECIFIC WIRING IMPLEMENTATION FOR PROPER STEPPER OPERATION"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.954 62.992 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "db994e30-73e9-40b7-85a0-14f17d618803")
	)
	(text "NOTES: (UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED)"
